00:00:07.423 --> 00:00:08.360
- Great.
- Great updates.

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:09.810
- [Joanna] It was that time again.

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:11.960
Apple's superlative mania

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:13.040
or what the company calls

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:15.210
its Worldwide Developers Conference.

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:16.130
At the virtual event,

00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:17.880
the company announced updates to.

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:20.279
- Our new release is iOS 15.

00:00:20.279 --> 00:00:21.112
- watchOS.

00:00:21.112 --> 00:00:22.141
- iPadOS 15.

00:00:22.141 --> 00:00:23.510
macOS Monterey.

00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:24.670
- [Joanna] The updates
are coming this fall

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:26.610
to all your gadgets and of course,

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:28.897
Apple highlighted all the features as.

00:00:28.897 --> 00:00:31.130
- The incredible, incredible, incredible.

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:32.930
- [Joanna] But not
everything can be incredible

00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:34.330
and great and the best

00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:37.070
because well, that's not how it works.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:38.860
Here's my list of what I actually think

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:40.210
will be the best features,

00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:43.670
plus a few nods to what's
more on the meh side.

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:46.230
Number one, improved Zoom features.

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:48.690
I mean FaceTime, but you
can understand the confusion

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:51.320
since FaceTime in the
upcoming iOS, iPadOS,

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:54.120
and macOS upgrades has a grid view

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.520
and blurred backgrounds

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:56.750
and noise cancellation.

00:00:56.750 --> 00:00:58.387
- Me too.

00:00:58.387 --> 00:00:59.500
Let me fix this.

00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:02.360
Better, right?

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:03.760
- [Joanna] Just like Zoom

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:06.250
but what Zoom doesn't have is SharePlay.

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:08.420
This FaceTime feature
let's you watch video

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:10.140
or listen to a song with the person

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:11.680
on the other end of the call.

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:13.860
For video sharing, it
will work with Disney+,

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:16.090
Hulu, TikTok and more.

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:19.680
Seems exciting but oh,
Netflix, where art thou?

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:21.690
Also big, FaceTime links,

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:23.180
which lets you send a link to others

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:24.670
to join a FaceTime call,

00:01:24.670 --> 00:01:26.970
even if they're on Android or Windows.

00:01:26.970 --> 00:01:29.110
Number two, Focus features.

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:31.750
- Focus is a new way to match your device

00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:33.740
to your current mindset.

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:34.810
- [Joanna] Now you can set a mode

00:01:34.810 --> 00:01:37.280
to block out notifications
you don't wanna see

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:39.150
during different times of the day.

00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:40.040
You set this up

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:42.360
and can customize what gets through.

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:44.140
Apple will also use on-device learning

00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:45.680
to suggest apps and people

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:48.310
to let through or block
during those times.

00:01:48.310 --> 00:01:50.470
Frankly, it all looks a bit confusing.

00:01:50.470 --> 00:01:52.000
Even better, when you put your device

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:53.090
on Do Not Disturb,

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:55.200
it can inform others that you're busy,

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:57.390
just like an old school away message.

00:01:57.390 --> 00:02:01.090
Number three, Find My AirPods Pro and Max.

00:02:01.090 --> 00:02:03.340
Sorry, no regular AirPods for this.

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:06.570
Those now work with Apple's
Find My Network, which means.

00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:07.790
- [Narrator] Your AirPods simply send out

00:02:07.790 --> 00:02:09.260
a secure Bluetooth beacon

00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:12.070
that can be detected
by other Apple devices.

00:02:12.070 --> 00:02:14.510
They can relay your AirPods'
location to the network

00:02:14.510 --> 00:02:16.120
and then back to your Find My App.

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:17.400
- [Joanna] If you lose them close by,

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:18.360
you can play the sound

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:20.340
and use the proximity
feature to find them,

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:21.960
plus there's a new separation alert

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:23.697
if you leave your AirPods behind.

00:02:23.697 --> 00:02:25.380
(phone beeping)

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:27.800
Number four driver's license.

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:30.170
So your Apple Wallet has
already had your credit cards

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:31.590
or your transit cards.

00:02:31.590 --> 00:02:33.810
Now it can have your driver's license.

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:36.510
- This fall, you'll just
scan your driver's license

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:39.570
or state ID in participating US states.

00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:40.900
- [Joanna] But that's the big question.

00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:43.110
What are the participating US states?

00:02:43.110 --> 00:02:44.320
Apple wouldn't say yet.

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:46.940
Apple says the TSA's also
working to accept this

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:49.640
so you could use your
phone's ID at the airport.

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:50.610
Pretty cool.

00:02:50.610 --> 00:02:52.270
Number five, Weather.

00:02:52.270 --> 00:02:54.750
Don't lie, you use your iPhone's
Weather app possibly more

00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:55.870
than any other app

00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:57.780
and you know it can be a lot better.

00:02:57.780 --> 00:02:59.640
The new version will
have full weather maps

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:01.390
and will make sure it's always sunny

00:03:01.390 --> 00:03:02.260
wherever you are.

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:03.500
Just joking on that last part.

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:04.920
Apple has a lot of power

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:06.680
but not that much power.

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:09.230
Number six, easier iPad multitasking.

00:03:09.230 --> 00:03:11.100
You no longer need to remember some combo

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:14.040
of secret swipes to multitask on an iPad.

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:16.040
An icon shows up at the top of the screen

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:17.390
where you can tap to put something

00:03:17.390 --> 00:03:19.970
on the side of the screen
or in full screen mode.

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:23.040
Number seven, on-device
speech recognition.

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:24.840
Siri can now do a lot more:

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:27.386
launch apps, control
music, change settings

00:03:27.386 --> 00:03:29.810
without ever using an internet connection

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:32.910
because it processes all the
information on the device,

00:03:32.910 --> 00:03:35.470
as long as you have a
recent iPhone or iPad.

00:03:35.470 --> 00:03:36.810
That means that those tasks

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:38.780
should be a lot faster too.

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:40.300
It definitely looked a lot faster

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:42.670
in Apple's recorded demos.

00:03:42.670 --> 00:03:43.523
- Open Photos.

00:03:45.860 --> 00:03:46.763
Open Calendar.

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:50.440
- [Joanna] I will have to
try that out for myself.

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:52.550
Number eight, digital legacy.

00:03:52.550 --> 00:03:54.710
This one is near and dear to my heart.

00:03:54.710 --> 00:03:56.600
A new feature in the Apple ID controls

00:03:56.600 --> 00:03:58.650
will let you assign a legacy contact,

00:03:58.650 --> 00:03:59.870
so if you were to die,

00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:01.980
that person could access
your Apple account,

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:04.550
including photos and other information.

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:05.880
This is something other companies,

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:08.800
including Google and Facebook
have had for a while.

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:12.090
Number nine, Safari tab groups.

00:04:12.090 --> 00:04:14.650
In macOS Monterey, and iOS 15,

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:17.020
Safari lets you group tabs together.

00:04:17.020 --> 00:04:18.910
So say you have a bunch
of tabs you wanna save

00:04:18.910 --> 00:04:20.660
around your next trip.

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:22.780
You can save them on this side bar.

00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:25.210
I use a similar feature in
Microsoft's Edge browser

00:04:25.210 --> 00:04:26.043
and I love it.

00:04:26.043 --> 00:04:28.370
This really may get me
to go back to Safari.

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:30.590
And speaking of Safari and iOS 15,

00:04:30.590 --> 00:04:32.800
the address bar is moved to the bottom.

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:34.840
That's gonna take some getting used to.

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:37.830
Number 10, lots of privacy.

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:40.030
It's hard to pick just
one privacy feature.

00:04:40.030 --> 00:04:42.010
There's a new service called Private Relay

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:44.250
that encrypts all your traffic in Safari.

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:45.420
To get it, you have to pay

00:04:45.420 --> 00:04:47.080
for another iCloud service though,

00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:49.020
which is called iCloud+.

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:50.750
Another that doesn't cost extra,

00:04:50.750 --> 00:04:52.070
the App Privacy Report,

00:04:52.070 --> 00:04:53.890
which is located in settings.

00:04:53.890 --> 00:04:55.620
- [Narrator] You can
see how often apps use

00:04:55.620 --> 00:04:56.980
the permission you've granted

00:04:56.980 --> 00:04:59.624
to access your location, photos,

00:04:59.624 --> 00:05:03.460
camera, microphone, contacts and more

00:05:03.460 --> 00:05:05.190
during the last seven days.

00:05:05.190 --> 00:05:06.023
- [Joanna] That sort of stuff used

00:05:06.023 --> 00:05:07.920
to require special software to see.

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:09.820
So yeah, those are my top picks.

00:05:09.820 --> 00:05:10.710
But some of the other stuff,

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:14.250
like improved photos on
a tiny, tiny watch screen

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:15.660
or a feature that tells me

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:17.016
when to get off the train

00:05:17.016 --> 00:05:18.920
or interactive memories

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:20.770
where you can add music to photos

00:05:20.770 --> 00:05:24.073
for an instant video, I'm not so sure.

00:05:24.073 --> 00:05:25.690
I look forward to testing it all

00:05:25.690 --> 00:05:28.610
before these operating systems
are released in the fall.

00:05:28.610 --> 00:05:30.360
In the meantime, just remember,

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:32.340
every feature cannot be.

00:05:32.340 --> 00:05:33.173
- The best.
- Best.

00:05:33.173 --> 00:05:34.280
- Best.
- Best.

00:05:34.280 --> 00:05:35.113
- Best.
- Best.

